      "output_preview": "## Business Logic Phase Complete\n\n### What was accomplished\n\n**`team-test/services.py`** \u2014 Production-ready business logic layer (691 lines) implementing `TaskService`, the single orchestration entry-point for the Task Management CLI tool.\n\n#### Key design decisions:\n- **Lazy loading**: task list is only read from disk on first access, avoiding unnecessary I/O\n- **Auto-save**: every mutating operation automatically persists to disk via `TaskStorage`\n- **Short-ID support**: all task-lookup methods accept both full UUIDs and 8-char short IDs\n- **Mirrors storage.py patterns**: uses the same `importlib`-based dynamic import so it works without a package setup\n\n#### Public API delivered:\n- **Exceptions**: `ServiceError`, `TaskNotFoundError`, `DuplicateTaskError`\n- **CRUD**: `create_task()`, `get_task()`, `update_task()`, `delete_task()`\n- **Status transitions**: `complete_task()`, `cancel_task()`, `start_task()`\n- **Querying**: `list_tasks()` (with status/priority/tag/overdue/search filters + 4 sort keys), `get_overdue_tasks()`, `search_tasks()`\n- **Statistics**: `get_statistics()` (counts by status, priority, overdue)\n- **Bulk operations**: `bulk_complete()`, `bulk_delete()` (skip-not-found semantics)\n- **Storage helpers**: `reload()`, `backup()`, `storage_path`, `task_count`\n\n**`team-test/test_services.py`** \u2014 Comprehensive test suite (119 tests, all passing).\n\n#### Test coverage:\n- Exception hierarchy and attributes\n- All CRUD operations (happy path + error paths)\n- All status transitions (complete/cancel/start) with persistence verification\n- `list_tasks()`: every filter type, all 4 sort keys, ascending/descending, combined filters, invalid sort_by\n- `get_overdue_tasks()`: filtering, ordering, terminal-status exclusion\n- `search_tasks()`: title, description, case-insensitive\n- `get_statistics()`: all status/priority keys, overdue count, empty state\n- `bulk_complete()` / `bulk_delete()`: all found, partial, none found, empty list, short IDs\n- `reload()`: lazy-load and",
